# WSL/Windows mark-of-the-web download artifacts
*:Zone.Identifier

# npm
node_modules/

# Build artifacts - regenerate with `bun run build`
data/page_inventory.json
data/page_inventory.csv

# Karl transcripts (`bun run export:karl`), generated from pages/*.js and the
# panel inventory in js/karl/karl-blocks.js. Never hand-edited, and stale the moment
# page copy changes. The reviewer-facing path is the Help-tab panel, which
# renders the same transcript with that browser's own edits applied; this
# directory is the whole-corpus snapshot for someone working from a checkout.
/review/karl-transcripts/

# Self-contained single-file export (`bun run build:singlefile`). Produced by
# vite-plugin-singlefile, which replaced the hand-rolled script/style
# concatenation that used to emit manager-review-single-file.html and
# single-file-export-current-source.html at the repo root.
/dist-singlefile/

# Those two root-level exports, which linger in older working copies. Nothing
# regenerates them any more — the script that did was deleted with the Vite
# migration — so these patterns keep leftover copies out of `git status`
# rather than ignoring a live build output, and can be dropped once no working
# copy still has them. `.prettierignore` lists the same two files.
/manager-review-single-file.html
/single-file-export-current-source.html

# Local dev SQLite DB for the optional /api/review-state sync backend
# (server.ts). Production points DATA_DB_PATH at a Railway volume instead.
/.data/

# Netlify deploy bundle (root only). Anchored with a leading slash on purpose:
# a bare "dist/" would also match forms/mosquito-workshop-request/dist/, whose
# built output IS committed (build:netlify copies it verbatim instead of
# running Vite). An unanchored pattern previously swallowed that sub-app's
# rebuilt hashed JS asset and shipped a form shell that never hydrated.
/dist/
.netlify

# Playwright
test-results/
playwright-report/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local scratch / one-off migration scripts and repo-dump artifacts. Root
# scratch files (scratch.js, fix_*.py, etc.) and repomix output were once
# committed by accident; keep them out of the tree — real tooling belongs
# in build_scripts/.
scratch*.js
repomix-output.xml

# Superpowers brainstorming scratch (mockups, session state)
.superpowers/

# Superpowers git worktrees (isolated workspaces for plan execution)
.worktrees/

# Google service account keys (never commit)
*-service-account*.json
google-service-account.json
.env.local

# Playwright MCP scratch console logs/snapshots (not part of source, see CLAUDE.md)
.playwright-mcp/

# Firecrawl CLI per-repo scrape cache. The CLI writes fetched pages here the
# first time `firecrawl scrape`/`search` runs from this directory — third-party
# web content, not source, and it grows without bound across sessions.
# (Credentials live in ~/.config/firecrawl-cli, not here.)
.firecrawl/

# Local tool settings/credentials
.poolside/
.karl-session.json
.karl-cookies.json

# Serena's per-machine project index and language-server config. It is written
# on first use by whichever agent has Serena attached, describes that machine's
# paths, and carries no facts about this repo a reader needs — so it is local
# tooling state rather than repo content.
.serena/

# Claude Code rewrites this file itself as permissions are granted, so its
# formatting is not ours to own. It is already in .prettierignore (added in
# #111); keep both lists in step so it neither shows in `git status` nor
# fails `bun run format:check` on a Claude Code machine.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Stray Windows-absolute-path artifacts written into the repo root by a
# Lighthouse MCP tool bug (e.g. "C:\Users\<name>\AppData\...\lighthouse.*"
# created verbatim as a literal directory name since WSL doesn't parse
# backslashes as path separators). Not real repo content if it recurs.
/C:*
# The same bug also emits a UNC-shaped variant when the tool resolves an
# undefined home directory against the WSL share — a literal directory named
# "\\wsl.localhost\Ubuntu\...\undefined\...\lighthouse.<id>". The /C:* rule
# above cannot match it, since that name starts with backslashes rather than a
# drive letter, so it showed up as untracked noise in every `git status`.
/\\*

# Project-local SQLite scratch dirs created by the server integration tests
# (tests/review-api-server.test.js, tests/ai-assist-server.test.js). Both call
# mkdtempSync against the REPO ROOT rather than the host temp dir, deliberately,
# so a failed run's database is still there to investigate. The cost of that
# choice is that git can see them, and a `git add -A` while a suite is running
# will commit one — which is exactly how a 6 MB review-state.db reached a
# feature branch. Anchored so they only match at the root, where they are made.
/.review-api-*/
/.ai-api-*/
agent-evals-regression-gate.zip

# JetBrains Junie's local copy of the agent skills. Unlike `.cursor/`,
# `.codex/` and `.claude/`, which carry a handful of deliberately tracked
# pointer files (see "Cross-tool canon" in AGENTS.md), this one is a
# generated 274-file duplicate of skills the repo already tracks under
# `.claude/skills/`, so nothing here is worth reviewing or versioning.
# It also has to be ignored rather than merely left untracked: Prettier 3
# reads `.gitignore` as well as `.prettierignore`, and 206 of these files
# fail `format:check` — enough to bury the handful of real findings the
# lint step exists to surface.
.junie/

